nd expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Georgia remains one of the closest states on the presidential map, with a partisan lean of roughly one point toward Republicans. The 2028 contest is an open-seat race, since the incumbent president is term-limited, which removes the usual incumbency effects for both parties.\n\nNo general-election polls, expert ratings, or fundraising figures are available yet, and recent headlines focus on Democratic primary speculation rather than the state's general-election dynamics. That leaves the race rated as a genuine tossup with a slight Republican tilt and unusually wide uncertainty. Early polling about prospective national candidates does not yet speak to how Georgia's electorate will behave in the general election.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4567, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4683, "margin": -1.0}]}